  "title": "Coast Guard rescues 2 from sinking vessel off Oahu",
  "description": "Two men are safe after being rescued by the Coast Guard off their sinking vessel 35 miles east of Kaneohe Bay early Friday morning. \r\n\r\nThe captain of the 82-foot pleasure craft, Point Harris, notified Coast Guard Sector Honolulu Command Center at 12:40 a.m. and reported they were taking on water in two forward water-tight compartments.\r\n\r\nThe two men were unable to energize the on-board dewatering pumps. They activated their emergency position indicating radio beacon and were preparing to abandon ship.",
